# Canonical line endings.
#
# One form in the repository: LF. The working tree uses LF for every text
# file, so a diff is always a real content change and never a line-ending
# artefact. Windows batch scripts are the single exception, because cmd.exe
# label and GOTO handling is not safe with LF-only endings.
#
# `text=auto` means git detects binary content and leaves it untouched; `eol=lf`
# pins the checkout form so the working tree does not depend on core.autocrlf
# or on which machine the clone happens on.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary. Never line-ending normalised. Listed explicitly rather than left to
# content detection, so a future editor or export that changes a file's bytes
# cannot silently convert an image or a jar into text.
*.jar  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
